# Files under /pinepods that are KNOWINGLY taken from the base image
# rather than from PINEPODS_COMMIT.
#
# The build fails if the real divergence set stops matching this file, in
# either direction: something new drifting, or something listed here no
# longer drifting. That is deliberate. The failure that produced this
# guard was silent -- a Rust API from September querying a June schema --
# and it surfaced only because a human noticed podcasts had stopped
# updating a day later.
#
# To accept a new divergence, add the path here with a comment saying why
# the base image's copy is the right one. To fix it instead, add a
# COPY --from=api-builder line for it in the Dockerfile.
#
# startup/ is NOT copied from the commit on purpose: startup.sh grew from
# 8951 to 12403 bytes between the base image (0.9.0, 2026-06-26) and the
# pinned commit (2026-09-09), and it orchestrates nginx, horust and the
# python entrypoint against tooling that the base image installed. Running
# September's orchestration against June's runtime is a bigger risk than
# the drift it would close. Revisit when the base image is bumped.
startup/nginx.conf
startup/startup.sh

# Arch packaging metadata for the desktop client. Never read, never
# executed inside this container; it is in the repo for AUR publishing.
clients/aur/.SRCINFO
clients/aur/PKGBUILD

# Differs from the commit by one entry: YTDLP_PATH = "${YTDLP_PATH}".
# Copying it would be worse than leaving it. June's startup.sh never sets
# YTDLP_PATH, so the variable would expand empty and hand the API an empty
# path instead of no path at all. yt-dlp is already on PATH at
# /usr/local/bin/yt-dlp, and there are zero IsYouTubeChannel podcasts
# configured, so nothing currently depends on it. Copy this file, and
# whatever sets the variable, when the base image is bumped to a release
# that carries the September startup.sh.
startup/services/pinepods-api.toml
